#N canvas 0 50 1040 1080 12;
#X text 30 16 =^..^=   datamod~   version 1 (2026)   sofia vallejo budziszewski   iem kug graz austria;
#X text 30 46 data modulators;
#X text 30 86 turns data into four control signals. any data series (a csv column or a list) plays as an lfo. there are also a lorenz attractor and a henon map and a cellular automaton with all 256 rules, f 110;
#X text 30 146 --- how it was made ---;
#X text 30 190 the lorenz system is integrated per sample with runge kutta. the henon map and the automaton step at the chosen rate. a series is read with hold or linear or cubic interpolation. all lanes are smoothed with a one pole filter, f 110;
#X text 30 270 --- how to use ---;
#X text 30 314 1  open the engine page. the four lanes drive an oscillator and show the data, f 110;
#X text 30 344 2  choose a source. lorenz and henon need no data, f 110;
#X text 30 374 3  send read file.csv 2 to play the second column of a csv file as an lfo, f 110;
#X text 30 404 4  connect the data outlet to the left inlet of any tessera effect and map it with datamap, f 110;
#X text 30 434 everything is a message: see the messages page for the full list and the examples page for patches to copy. every effect has presets and a and b morph and mutate and a data inlet, f 110;
#X text 30 494 try:  rate means different things: traversals per second for a series and time units per second for lorenz and steps per second for henon and ca, f 110;
#X text 30 544 try:  set clock to external and send step to drive the automaton from your own metro, f 110;
#X text 30 574 try:  the cells outlet message gives the first 16 cells of the automaton row as a pattern, f 110;
#X text 30 618 --- common problems ---;
#X text 30 662 read failed: the path is relative to the patch folder. use an absolute path or put the file next to the patch, f 110;
#X text 30 712 series is flat: the column has no variation or you chose a text column, f 110;
#X text 30 742 no output: sources step by the clock. check rate and that dsp is on, f 110;
#X text 30 772 names: give every instance its own name as the first argument like [tessera/datamod~ d1]. the name is also the stash namespace, f 110;
#X text 30 836 --- click a box to open that page ---;
#N canvas 0 50 900 974 presets 0;
#X text 30 16 factory sounds are stored as plain text. click a box to load that sound. every slider in the effect follows, f 100;
#X text 30 66 --- factory presets ---;
#X msg 30 110 \; d1 preset 0;
#X text 240 112 0  default;
#X msg 30 144 \; d1 preset 1;
#X text 240 146 1  lorenz drift;
#X msg 30 178 \; d1 preset 2;
#X text 240 180 2  lorenz fast;
#X msg 30 212 \; d1 preset 3;
#X text 240 214 3  henon steps;
#X msg 30 246 \; d1 preset 4;
#X text 240 248 4  henon edge;
#X msg 460 110 \; d1 preset 5;
#X text 670 112 5  rule 30 gates;
#X msg 460 144 \; d1 preset 6;
#X text 670 146 6  rule 90 tree;
#X msg 460 178 \; d1 preset 7;
#X text 670 180 7  rule 110 grid;
#X msg 460 212 \; d1 preset 8;
#X text 670 214 8  series loop;
#X text 30 300 --- now playing ---;
#X symbolatom 30 344 20 0 0 0 - d1-name -;
#X floatatom 230 344 4 0 0 0 - d1-index -;
#X text 340 346 name and number (minus one means edited);
#X msg 30 388 \; d1 next;
#X msg 142 388 \; d1 prev;
#X msg 254 388 \; d1 mutate 0.3;
#X text 30 428 next and prev step through the presets and wrap around. mutate varies the current sound by a random amount from 0 to 1. mutate leaves mix and level alone, f 100;
#X text 30 478 --- morph between two sounds ---;
#X msg 30 522 \; d1 A;
#X msg 118 522 \; d1 B;
#X text 206 524 a and b remember the current sound;
#X text 30 564 morph;
#X obj 110 562 hsl 300 18 0 1 0 0 d1-morph empty empty -2 -8 0 12 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X text 30 606 load one preset and press a then load another and press b then move the morph slider. every continuous parameter blends smoothly. switches change at the middle, f 100;
#X text 30 656 --- your own user bank ---;
#X msg 30 700 \; d1 store mysound;
#X msg 214 700 \; d1 save my.bank;
#X msg 390 700 \; d1 load my.bank;
#X text 30 740 store keeps the current sound after the factory presets. save writes the user bank to a text file next to this patch and load reads such a file, f 100;
#X text 30 790 --- presets with stash ---;
#X text 30 834 every slider of the effect sends to d1-param and listens on d1-param-r. this is the naming scheme of the stash preset library: create [stash/bank d1] and send it a scan message with the name of the patch that holds the effect. it follows the stash rules but has not been tested together yet, f 100;
#X restore 30 880 pd presets;
#X text 30 914 all sounds and morph, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1200 714 parameters 0;
#X text 30 16 every parameter is also a message: [name value( in real units or for a switch the option name or number. the controls in the effect panel and these messages do the same, f 120;
#X text 30 66 parameter;
#X text 210 66 values;
#X text 560 66 what it does;
#X text 30 100 source;
#X text 210 100 series | lorenz | henon | ca, f 36;
#X text 560 100 series or lorenz or henon or ca, f 54;
#X text 30 136 rate;
#X text 210 136 0.02 to 200 log, f 36;
#X text 560 136 speed. see the tips, f 54;
#X text 30 172 smooth;
#X text 210 172 0 to 2000, f 36;
#X text 560 172 smoothing time of the lanes in ms, f 54;
#X text 30 208 depth;
#X text 210 208 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 208 scales the output around the middle, f 54;
#X text 30 244 offset;
#X text 210 244 -1 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 244 shifts the output, f 54;
#X text 30 280 bipolar;
#X text 210 280 off | on, f 36;
#X text 560 280 on gives -1 to 1 instead of 0 to 1, f 54;
#X text 30 316 interp;
#X text 210 316 hold | linear | cubic, f 36;
#X text 560 316 series interpolation: hold or linear or cubic, f 54;
#X text 30 352 loop;
#X text 210 352 once | loop | pingpong, f 36;
#X text 560 352 series end behaviour: once or loop or pingpong, f 54;
#X text 30 388 chaos;
#X text 210 388 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 388 lorenz rho and henon a. higher is wilder, f 54;
#X text 30 424 rule;
#X text 210 424 0 to 255, f 36;
#X text 560 424 cellular automaton rule 0 to 255, f 54;
#X text 30 460 width;
#X text 210 460 8 to 64 whole numbers, f 36;
#X text 560 460 number of automaton cells (8 to 64), f 54;
#X text 30 496 density;
#X text 210 496 0 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 496 fill of the first automaton row after a reseed, f 54;
#X text 30 532 clock;
#X text 210 532 internal | external, f 36;
#X text 560 532 internal or external (send step), f 54;
#X text 30 568 warp;
#X text 210 568 -1 to 1, f 36;
#X text 560 568 bends the shape of the output, f 54;
#X text 30 614 any continuous parameter can be driven by data: send datamap name amount and then data 0 to 1. see the messages page, f 120;
#X restore 220 880 pd parameters;
#X text 220 914 every control, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 956 messages 0;
#X text 30 16 click any box to send it to the effect. the effect listens to its name so you can use [s d1] from anywhere in your patch, f 110;
#X text 30 66 message;
#X text 430 66 what it does;
#X msg 30 100 \; d1 params;
#X text 430 102 prints every parameter and its range in the console, f 76;
#X msg 30 134 \; d1 preset 3;
#X text 430 136 loads preset 3 (or a preset by name: preset lorenz drift), f 76;
#X msg 30 168 \; d1 next;
#X text 430 170 next preset (wraps around), f 76;
#X msg 30 202 \; d1 prev;
#X text 430 204 previous preset, f 76;
#X msg 30 236 \; d1 mutate 0.4;
#X text 430 238 random variation of the current sound. 0 is nothing and 1 is a lot, f 76;
#X msg 30 270 \; d1 A;
#X text 430 272 remember the current sound as a, f 76;
#X msg 30 304 \; d1 B;
#X text 430 306 remember the current sound as b, f 76;
#X msg 30 338 \; d1 morph 0.5;
#X text 430 340 blend between a and b from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 372 \; d1 data 0.7;
#X text 430 374 data inlet: a value from 0 to 1, f 76;
#X msg 30 406 \; d1 datamap rate 0.5;
#X text 430 408 map the data inlet to a continuous parameter. 0.5 means the full range of the parameter at data 0 and 1. amount 0 removes the mapping. up to four mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 480 \; d1 datamap clear;
#X text 430 482 remove all data mappings, f 76;
#X msg 30 514 \; d1 store mysound;
#X text 430 516 keep the current sound in the user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 548 \; d1 save my.bank;
#X text 430 550 write the user bank to a text file, f 76;
#X msg 30 582 \; d1 load my.bank;
#X text 430 584 read a user bank, f 76;
#X msg 30 616 \; d1 read data.csv 2;
#X text 430 618 plays column 2 of a csv or text file (header lines are skipped). the path is relative to the patch, f 76;
#X msg 30 670 \; d1 series 1 5 2 8 3;
#X text 430 672 plays a list as the series, f 76;
#X msg 30 704 \; d1 array mytable;
#X text 430 706 plays a pd array, f 76;
#X msg 30 738 \; d1 seed 7;
#X text 430 740 restarts the chaos sources from a seed, f 76;
#X msg 30 772 \; d1 restart;
#X text 430 774 series back to the start, f 76;
#X msg 30 806 \; d1 step;
#X text 430 808 advances henon or ca by one step (use with clock external), f 76;
#X msg 30 840 \; d1 reseed;
#X text 430 842 fills the first automaton row at random with the density param, f 76;
#X msg 30 874 \; d1 cells 32;
#X text 430 876 automaton with one single cell in the middle, f 76;
#X restore 410 880 pd messages;
#X text 410 914 clickable list, f 22;
#N canvas 0 50 1300 1000 examples 0;
#X text 30 16 copy these into your own patch. they all talk to the effect through [s d1] so the engine page must be open with dsp on, f 130;
#X text 30 56 1  walk through the presets;
#X obj 30 90 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 30 130 metro 2500;
#X obj 30 170 random 9;
#X obj 30 210 list prepend preset;
#X obj 30 250 list trim;
#X obj 30 290 s d1;
#X text 330 56 2  slow morph between preset 0 and 1;
#X msg 330 90 \; d1 preset 0 \; d1 A \; d1 preset 1 \; d1 B;
#X obj 330 150 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 330 190 metro 6000;
#X msg 330 230 0 \, 1 3000 \, 0 3000 3000;
#X obj 330 270 line 0 30;
#X obj 330 310 list prepend morph;
#X obj 330 350 list trim;
#X obj 330 390 s d1;
#X text 740 56 3  sweep rate with a ramp;
#X obj 740 90 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 740 130 metro 4000;
#X msg 740 170 0.2 \, 8 2000 \, 0.2 2000 2000;
#X obj 740 210 line 0.2 30;
#X obj 740 250 list prepend rate;
#X obj 740 290 list trim;
#X obj 740 330 s d1;
#X text 30 496 4  data in: a ramp stands in for a sensor or a csv column. click the map box once first;
#X msg 30 530 \; d1 datamap rate 0.4;
#X obj 30 570 tgl 18 0 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -262144 -1 -1 0 1;
#X obj 30 610 metro 4000;
#X msg 30 650 0 \, 1 2000 \, 0 2000 2000;
#X obj 30 690 line 0 30;
#X obj 30 730 list prepend data;
#X obj 30 770 list trim;
#X obj 30 810 s d1;
#X text 330 570 in your own patch send any value from 0 to 1 to [s d1] as: data 0.7. for a csv series scale it to the range 0 to 1 first. [tessera/datamod~] does that for you and its data outlet can be connected straight to the inlet of any tessera effect, f 70;
